{"conversation_id":"ae995f44-d5a3-484c-82b4-695a353f4cd8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-22 07:12:58 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-22 14:12:58 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\nCoding-Agent: agy\nSession-ID: ae995f44-d5a3-484c-82b4-695a353f4cd8\n\nFindings written to [1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/collab/yang-clojure/1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md).\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **NOTE | [contract.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/contract.cljc#L240) | Optional `:kind` default in `frontend-contract` projection grants:**\n   `yang.core.semantics/validate-descriptor` ([semantics.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/core/semantics.cljc#L249)) defaults an omitted projection `:kind` to `:cell-accessor` (`{:keys [module export kind] :or {kind :cell-accessor}}`) per [yang.preludes.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/docs/design/yang.preludes.md#L433-L435) §6.3, whereas `contract/frontend-contract` ([contract.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/contract.cljc#L240)) destructures `{:keys [module export kind]}` without `:or {kind :cell-accessor}`. All entries in `contract/clojure-projections` ([contract.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/contract.cljc#L205-L215)) specify `:kind :cell-accessor` explicitly, so no built-in or tested projection is affected.\n\n2. **NOTE | [module.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L157-L162), [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L135-L136), [query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc#L176) | Child-namespace trie collision and falsy export resolution fixes:**\n   Linking `clojure.core.impl` before `clojure.core` creates the intermediate trie path `['clojure 'core]` with `:children {'impl ...}` before `clojure.core` itself is installed. Switching `resolve-module` existence checks to `module-entry` ([module.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L646), [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1537), [query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc#L176)) and adding `module/export-binding` ([module.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L157-L162)) cleanly resolves both dependency-first linking of dotted parent/child module names and `:kind :value` exports whose values are `nil`, `false`, or `:clj/unbound`, without touching `yin.vm.provenance-scope` or weakening P1′ provenance-door enforcement.\n\n## Review Focus Summary\n\n- **§6.4 validation authority ([semantics.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/core/semantics.cljc#L106-L267)):** Verified language-agnostic schema validation, address-verified closure \u0026 semantic-bytecode row verification, namespace qualification (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook`) across hooks and `:overflow-op`, closure export membership (`:export`), `:lambda` definition check (`:non-lambda`), signature-vs-`:call-shapes` check against `entry-lowering` (`:arity`), `:cell-accessor` (`0`-arg lambda target + `0`-arg `init!` + `1`-arg `export`) and `:value` (`:literal`) projection checks, reserved-door ban (`cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, `*.impl/*`), and address-bound role tuple `[address target role]` (`:export-role`), with same-module wrong-role substitution tested in [descriptor_profile_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/test/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc#L80-L145) (`clj.py/sub` for `:op/add`, `clj.py/neg` for `:int :overflow-op`, `clojure.core/dec` for `\"inc\"`).\n- **Legacy `py-v1` behavior preservation ([lower.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc), [contract.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/contract.cljc#L138-L151)):** 1:1 `'py/*` hook mapping, frozen 1-arg `py/run-main` entry shape, untouched `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, and unchanged legacy golden roots.\n- **`clj.py` per §7.3 ([clj_runtime.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/clj_runtime.cljc#L13-L305)):** 5-arg `clj.py/make-fn` → `clj/make-callable`, `clj.py/call` → `clj/invoke-callable`, zero provenance doors (excluded from `:trusted-prelude-modules`), boxed float operations throughout, and 2-arg `clj.py/run-main` / `clj.py/run-session` installing `clj.py/_policy` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `try-finally` context restoration and verbatim return values.\n- **The DEFAULT flip (§6.5) ([frontend.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc#L204-L229), [frontends.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc#L301-L399), [repl.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L205-L215), [profiles.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/profiles.cljc#L186-L274)):** `:yang.frontend/preferred [:yang/python \"clojure-core-v1\"]` resolves ID-only `:yang/python` requests to `\"clojure-core-v1\"` while preserving explicit `[:yang/python \"py-v1\"]` pins and in-flight session snapshots; descriptor/runtime pins reconcile by module symbol before lowering; compilation derivation records (including `:yang.frontend/runtime-closure` and `:yang.frontend/ambient-resolver`) are recorded in `:frontend-derivations`.\n- **§9 P3′ gates in fixtures ([descriptor_profile_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/dw-p3prime/test/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc#L159-L397)):** Real cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind with an unrelated `:effect` handler in path asserts exact-once cleanup and nonzero `:depth`/`:base` context restoration across `:bundled`/`:linked` × `:semantic`/`:stack`/`:register`; capability refusals fail closed before emission; all four r8 default-profile regressions (`:k` admission, cross-carrier integer key identity on insert and lookup, `:clj/unbound` value vs absent binding distinguishability, Jing encoded-byte canonical order `0` before `nil`) are verified.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED\n","duration_seconds":441.397673,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":213064,"output_tokens":27100,"thinking_tokens":19906,"cache_read_tokens":2485787,"total_tokens":240164}}
